ohsdigi - third-party code linked into the built module
=======================================================

ohsdigi itself (rust/ohsdigi) is free software under the GNU General Public
License, version 3 or later, as the rest of OpenHamShack NB and OpenHamShack HAM.
Much of it is ported from WSJT-X 2.7.0 (GPL-3.0-or-later), copyright (C)
2001-2023 Joe Taylor K1JT, Steve Franke K9AN, Bill Somerville G4WJS, Nico
Palermo IV3NWV and the WSJT Development Group; each ported file names the
WSJT-X files it follows. https://wsjt.sourceforge.io/

Its JS8 module (src/js8) is ported from JS8Call 2.2.0 (GPL-3.0-or-later),
copyright (C) 2018-2020 Jordan Sherer KN4CRD, itself a fork of WSJT-X 1.9
by the authors above; https://github.com/js8call/js8call. src/js8/jsc.bin.gz
is JS8Call's word-compression dictionary (jsc_map.cpp, jsc_list.cpp) in a
compact form, made by harness/gen_js8_tables.py.

Its HSmodem module (src/hsmodem, the QO-100 multimedia beacon's modem) is
ported from HSmodem, copyright (C) Kurt Moraw DJ0ABR, GPL version 2 or
later (its file headers; GPL-3.0 in its repository),
https://github.com/amsat-dl/QO-100-Modem, and from liquid-dsp, whose
notice follows; the MIT licence text below applies to it.

    liquid-dsp
        Copyright (c) 2007 - 2020 Joseph Gaeddert
        https://github.com/jgaeddert/liquid-dsp (and DJ0ABR's fork,
        https://github.com/dj0abr/liquid-dsp, which HSmodem ships)

The built module (ohsdigi.abi3.so on Linux, ohsdigi.pyd on Windows) also
contains, compiled in, the following Rust crates, each offered under the
MIT licence or the Apache License 2.0 at the user's choice; they are used
here under the MIT licence, whose text follows. Their exact versions are
pinned in rust/ohsdigi/Cargo.lock.

    PyO3 0.29.3, pyo3-ffi 0.29.3
        Copyright (c) 2023-present PyO3 Project and Contributors.
        https://github.com/PyO3/pyo3
    libc 0.2.190
        Copyright (c) The Rust Project Developers.
        https://github.com/rust-lang/libc
    once_cell 1.21.4
        Copyright (c) Aleksey Kladov.
        https://github.com/matklad/once_cell
    flate2 1.1.10, miniz_oxide 0.9.1, crc32fast 1.5.2, adler2 2.0.1
        (unpacking src/js8/jsc.bin.gz)
        Copyright (c) Alex Crichton, Frommi, oyvindln, Sam Rijs and
        contributors. https://github.com/rust-lang/flate2-rs
    fancy-regex 0.14.0, regex-automata 0.4.18, regex-syntax 0.8.11,
    aho-corasick 1.1.5, memchr 2.8.3, bit-set 0.8.0, bit-vec 0.8.0
        (JS8Call's text patterns, src/js8/varicode.rs)
        Copyright (c) The fancy-regex authors, The Rust Project
        Developers, Andrew Gallant, Alexis Beingessner and contributors.
        https://github.com/fancy-regex/fancy-regex,
        https://github.com/rust-lang/regex
    The Rust standard library (Rust 1.98.1)
        Copyright (c) The Rust Project Contributors.
        https://github.com/rust-lang/rust

Other crates in Cargo.lock (proc-macro2, quote, syn, heck, unicode-ident,
pyo3-macros, pyo3-build-config) run only while compiling and are not part
of the built module.

